      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "To clarify, such a system would ONLY be needed when you want to dynamically construct URLs at runtime for a non-whitelisted domain. Then it would make sense, yes. But because this canny here doesn't describe it as that being the main factor, it feels wrong to me.",
