      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "65f4b8e96c51e1792144f180",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "> When a world has required permissions, the user must accept those permissions in order to be able to join the world.\n\nI disagree on that, too easy to get to warning fatigue, especially if the pop-up is provided by VRChat. I think if worlds can check permissions at run time, it'll be easy for them to explain to users what they want and hopefully why.\n\nI have been in one world that actually checks if untrusted urls are enabled. Only noticed that because a friend that reset a bunch of things. I'd guess they just use the string loader and if it falls, show the pop-up.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
